   "notes": "Staged second-order Birch-Murnaghan P-V-T parameterization from Martinez et al. (1996). Each Table 6 isotherm fixes K0'=4; Equation (2) supplies the reported linear K0(T) slope, and Equation (3) uses the reported mean expansion coefficient in the direct relation V0(T)=V0(298 K)*[1+alpha_bar*(T-298 K)]. Table 6 reports the 298 K V0=227.5+/-0.8 A^3 and sigma(K0)=3.48 GPa; the prose and Table 7 instead summarize the K0 error as approximately 4.3 GPa. Table 6 contains fitted isotherms through 973 K. The source reports no parameter covariance or confidence convention, and the stored pressure/temperature extrema are an experimental envelope rather than a rectangular validity guarantee.",
